WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.460
(opening music plays)

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.960
NARRATOR: The gallbladder is a pear-shaped pouch underneath your liver.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.320
With the liver, it attaches to the small intestine through a series of tubes called ducts.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.040
Bile, a substance made by the liver to break down fat, is stored in the gallbladder.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.120
When fatty food from a meal reaches the small intestine,

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.080
the gallbladder releases bile into it to help digest the fat.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.720
Cholecystectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the gallbladder.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:59.220
It is usually done when there is evidence of gallbladder disease, such as gallstones...

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.240
...or polyps.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.280
It is also done for biliary dyskinesia, which is a condition where the gallbladder doesn't work properly.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:19.860
Laparoscopic cholecystectomy requires only small, keyhole incisions through the abdomen, known as ports.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.660
To reach the gallbladder, the surgeon will insert tubes called trocars through these ports.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.280
One port is usually located at the navel, or umbilicus.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:40.480
Carbon dioxide gas pumped through the umbilical port will inflate the abdomen, so its contents can be viewed more easily.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.980
Next, your surgeon will insert the laparoscope through the umbilical port.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.980
Images from its camera will be transmitted to a video monitor in the operating room.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:02.140
Using instruments passed through other ports, your surgeon will grasp the gallbladder, clip off its main artery and duct,

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.300
drop it into a specimen bag, and remove it through one of the ports.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:18.620
After the laparoscope is removed, a port value will be left in place briefly, to allow all of the carbon dioxide to escape from the abdomen.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:26.040
The incisions will be closed with sutures, followed by skin glue or skin closure tape.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:35.980
If there are complications with your laparoscopic procedure, your surgeon will switch to an open procedure with a larger incision.

